{
 "about": "Vectors for the x402/exact/cardano and x402/exact/cardano/lock pairings: the cardano entry point of @integraledger/lcp. H is SHA-256(\"abc\") from FIPS 180-2. V1 is cbor2 5.7.1's encoding of the auxiliary data (pycardano 0.19.2's AuxiliaryData(AlonzoMetadata(...)).to_cbor() is equal). V2 and V4 are built with pycardano 0.19.2 on Python 3.11; the one vkey witness is from a key generated when the fixture was built, which does not change the body or the id. V3 is Cardano preprod transaction 628eca29…c73ef4be, its CBOR read through Koios /tx_cbor on 2026-09-25; V4's row 14 is V3's transaction with a bit set past the last byte in its last base64 character before the padding. Every Blake2b-256 is Python's hashlib.blake2b(digest_size=32) over the item's bytes as located by cbor2's decoder. fixed.OLock is fixed.O under the `script` lock method, the option of x402/exact/cardano/lock. The V4 rows that carry auxiliaryDataHex were built with cbor2 5.7.1 and hashlib on Python 3.12.3: V2's body with key 7 set to the Blake2b-256 of the hand-assembled auxiliary data given, signed by the Ed25519 key of seed 00x32 (pycardano 0.19.2). CIP-20 lines are compared as their UTF-8 bytes: a repeated key in label 674's map, a repeated label 674, more than one line that reads as the marker when case and a leading byte-order mark (U+FEFF) are ignored, and a marker line not in lower case are each refused, because readers that keep the last of repeated keys (cborg 6.1.3's default decode) or strip a leading byte-order mark would read those messages another way; cborg 6.1.3 with rejectDuplicateMapKeys refuses each repeated-key row. V5's recover rows read the included transaction by its id. V6 is V2's transaction with body key 3 removed and the map's count lowered, its id Python's hashlib.blake2b(digest_size=32) over the new body: the address method admits a body with no TTL, as @x402/cardano 2.30.0's facilitator admits it (exact/facilitator/scheme.ts:815, which checks a TTL only where the body has one), and the lock refuses it, since the scheme requires a TTL of a lock (scheme_exact_cardano.md:836). V7 is the scheme's own Masumi datum encoding test vector, copied from scheme_exact_cardano.md (SHA-256 7079d96f…204e4968, line 514), whose field 2, the seller, is the enterprise address of key hash 22 x 28 (lines 497-513). V8 is the agreement floor, the formula of the scheme's Minimum UTXO Value (scheme_exact_cardano.md:899-902): its address bytes are BIP-173's reference Bech32 decoder's (github.com/sipa/bech32 ref/python/segwit_addr.py, without the 90-character limit) and each output is cborg 6.1.3's encoding of {0: address, 1: value}, its coin found by iterating from zero to the least coin that covers its own encoding; the token row's value is [coin, {policy: {empty name: 1}}]. The read's own rows, status over a ledger, are the read kit's (read-status.json through the forms in test/read-kit/forms/cardano.ts, over a constructed ledger, every answer of which is constructed and says so) and the constructed rows of test/cardano.test.ts. The agreedRefusals row for an inclusion above the tip reads 0 confirmations, below the 20 asked for: pending below-mark (rule 17).",
